WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.260
Reflections 501B OpenMOE matches GLM 5.2 reasoning at 123rd the active parameters. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 195. Reflection ai released Beam as its first open weight model. The system is a 501 billion parameter sparse mixture of experts design, with 23 billion active parameters. It targets coding and agentic workloads.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:35.520
beam reportedly matches GLM 5.2 on reasoning benchmarks, while using 3-4 times less inference compute.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.760
Apache 2.0 weights are scheduled for release later in October 2026.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.740
Nvidia provided backing for the project.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:50.640
Falcon Emirati 7B adapts the Falcon H1 Arabic base for Emirati dialect and culture.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:58.040
The model specializes in Emirati Arabic vocabulary, grammar, tone, and cultural context, including

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.160
Navati poetry.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:04.160
It builds on the 7 billion parameter variant of the Falcon H1 family.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.680
The Falcon H1 family uses a hybrid state space model and transformer attention architecture,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.220
running in parallel inside every block.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:20.620
The family supports context windows up to 256,000 tokens and was already trained on Gulf,

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:28.560
Levantine, Egyptian, and Magrebi dialects alongside MSA and English. The new swi-race benchmark draws

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:36.020
tasks from merged pull requests in roughly 100 Python projects. It grades fixes using each project's

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.280
own tests inside isolated containers

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:41.460
across 188 real concurrency bugs.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:47.440
GLM 5.3 Flash scored 85% with one attempt per task,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.140
and 82% with two to three attempts.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.020
Those scores placed GLM 5.3 Flash statistically tied

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.840
with GPT 5.6 Luna at 81%.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.700
Half the tasks prove easy for all models

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.640
while the remaining half drive most performance differences.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.840
South Korea plans to begin development of a frontier-scale AI model in 2027.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:16.240
The government has allocated a total budget of $3.5 billion for the effort.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:22.900
Open AI will begin watermarking eligible text from chat GPT and codex in the EU over the

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:23.560
coming weeks.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.700
A PI customers can enable text watermarking for select models worldwide immediately.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:35.480
The watermark embeds an invisible statistical signal detectable only by approved researchers

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:39.540
for now, because short passages and rewriting can remove it.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:47.160
API3 launched air node hub, so agents can discover, pay for, and verify APIs independently.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:53.040
The marketplace uses machine readable descriptions and cryptographic signatures on every response.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:03:00.540
Roughly 3 dozen services are listed at launch, spanning finance, weather, news, health, and mapping data.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:06.740
Each service sets its own per request price and providers retain customer relationships and branding.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:12.700
Memoria 1.0.0 releases a local model agnostic memory system.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:22.000
It runs FAAISS, BM25, graph retrieval, phrase matching, attribute retrieval, and temporal retrieval in parallel.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.040
then fuses signals through multi-signal ranking.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:36.240
On LongMemEVAL-S, it achieved 89.8% recall at 1 and 0.9257 session NDCG at 10, while using

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.140
an average peak RSS of 580 megabytes per query.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:49.780
Memoria supports GitHub and Obsidian ingestion, MCP, CLI, TUI, GUI and API plus a plug-in system

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.700
with 34 hooks and installs by a PIP.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:04:01.020
An analysis of 109 AI agent incidents found 38% of container escapes used trivial misconfigurations.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:07.700
Common vectors included mounting docker.sock into sandboxes, passing parent environment variables

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:13.840
to sub agents, missing taint tracking on tool outputs, and unconstrained local socket binding.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:19.840
Researches released an open-source multi-agent supervisor security harness with formal

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.980
taint propagation and boundary controls under Apache 2.0.

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:30.380
Trust gaps in the model context protocol allow malicious prompts to propagate between agents

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:31.540
from different vendors.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.260
The vulnerability affects systems from Google and others.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:42.480
LocalMind runs 37GB mixture of experts models in a browser tab via disk-streamed experts.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:48.260
The Static Web GPU page streams mixture of experts' weights from disk during generation

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.120
on a 24GB M4 Pro Mac.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:05:01.140
Gemma 426bA4b achieved 23.6 tokens per second decode, with output matching llama.cpp on

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:02.660
15 of 16 prompts.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:11.100
Overclocking DDR5 to 4,800 MHz improves MoE pre-fill and decode on llama.cpp.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:20.820
A 36% bandwidth increase on an AMD 7950X system raised pre-fill by approximately 10% and token

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:28.660
generation by 5% for models that do not fit in VRAM. Gaines grew deeper in context, reaching 14%

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:36.780
on 8000 pre-fill. GLM 5.3 Flash handles million-line production code bases at frontier speed,

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:42.340
A company using the model for daily software engineering work on very large repositories

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:48.900
reports strong performance on repo exploration, multi-file refactoring, and architecture tracing.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:56.960
Civ Bench controlled evaluation ranks GLM 5.3 ahead of Opus 5.5 in Civilization 5.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:02.580
The benchmark rotates three fixed starts across models with eight civilizations per game.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:10.820
GLM 5.3 secured cultural victories, while Quinn 3.8227B achieved science victories.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:17.800
Try Falcon Emirati 7B on hugging phase for Emirati Arabic tasks where standard MSA models

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:19.040
miscultural nuance.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:24.740
Run the sweet race tasks locally to compare your preferred coding agent against the published

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:29.600
GLM 5.3 Flash and GPT 5.6 Luna baselines.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:34.860
instructions. Install Memorial via PIP and point it at a local obsidian vault to test

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:42.620
multi-signal retrieval on your own notes. Load the Gemma 426 BA4BGGUF in the local mind

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:47.320
browser demo to see disc-streamed MOE performance on your own hardware.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:55.320
Apache 2.0 weights for Reflection Beam are expected later in October 2026. South Korea Frontier

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.360
model development is scheduled to begin in 2027.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.780
Further open AI text watermarking rollout for EU compliance

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:04.540
continues over the coming weeks.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:08.740
Let me pop the hood on the Falcon H1 hybrid block design.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.380
Falcon H1 places a state-space model path

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:15.540
and a transformer attention path inside every block

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.600
and fuses their outputs before the final projection.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:23.020
The Mamba-style SSM path processes long sequences

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:28.140
in linear time, while the accention path preserves precise long-range token interactions.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:34.260
This parallel design avoids the quadratic cost of full attention on extended contexts,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:39.020
yet retains the precision needed for morphologically rich languages such as Arabic.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:44.880
On sequences beyond 32,000 tokens, the hybrid block reduces memory traffic

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:50.300
compared with pure attention while keeping perplexity within 1% of a matched transformer.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:56.940
The approach adds roughly 15% parameters per block, but cuts inference latency by up to

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:59.900
40% on 128K contexts.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:06.500
Teams should prefer the hybrid block when context length exceeds 64K, and inference budget

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.240
is constrained.

